WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.741
"Look out!" Zann yelled. One of the giant jellyfish was moving straight toward Perda, its huge mouth gaping open.

2
00:00:08.742 --> 00:00:13.827
Rubbing his wet fingers together, Zann tried to send a Blast spell at the monster.

3
00:00:13.828 --> 00:00:17.229
But he could barely manage a small sizzle of energy.

4
00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:22.346
Still, he distracted the creature long enough for Perda to swim away from it.

5
00:00:22.347 --> 00:00:26.963
Zing dive-bombed the creatures, trying to blast them with his fiery breath.

6
00:00:26.964 --> 00:00:31.318
But he was too wet. Nothing but a small puff of steam came out.

7
00:00:31.319 --> 00:00:33.856
"Sing, Zing!" Darb yelled.

8
00:00:33.857 --> 00:00:38.977
Zing started whistling his hypnotic tune. Zann didn't know if it would work.

9
00:00:38.978 --> 00:00:43.820
He'd already seen that at least some otherworldly creatures weren't affected by it.

10
00:00:43.821 --> 00:00:47.698
These creatures didn't seem to be hypnotized by Zing's song either.

11
00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:50.327
But at least they did appear curious.

12
00:00:50.328 --> 00:00:56.069
They turned and swam after Zing, peering up at him with huge, watery eyes.

13
00:00:56.070 --> 00:01:00.026
"Hey!" a voice shouted from the other direction. "Heads up!"

14
00:01:00.027 --> 00:01:04.130
Zann turned and saw a long sailboat shooting toward them.

15
00:01:04.131 --> 00:01:09.831
Seconds later the boat arrived, and hands reached out to drag the kids aboard.

16
00:01:09.832 --> 00:01:16.076
"Hurry!" a man shouted in a gruff, urgent voice. "The gulpers are turning back."

17
00:01:16.077 --> 00:01:23.351
Stiff winds lifted the sails and carried the boat swiftly over the waves, leaving the monsters far behind.

18
00:01:23.352 --> 00:01:27.373
Moments later Zing caught up and landed beside Zann.

19
00:01:27.374 --> 00:01:31.829
The dragon was out of breath, panting out little bursts of steam.

20
00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:36.611
"Gulpers are always hungry, but luckily they're slow," someone said.

21
00:01:36.612 --> 00:01:41.223
Zann turned and saw a boy around his own age smiling at him.

22
00:01:41.224 --> 00:01:47.175
"Hi," Zann said. "Thanks for saving us. How did you know we needed help?"

23
00:01:47.176 --> 00:01:51.172
"We were fishing when we saw your strange bird flying around."

24
00:01:51.173 --> 00:01:55.093
The boy pointed at Zing. "We came to see what it was."

25
00:01:55.094 --> 00:02:01.478
"His name is Zing," Zann said. "He's a dragon. Oh, and I'm Zann."

26
00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:05.115
"My name's Ello," the other boy said. "Nice to meet you."

27
00:02:05.116 --> 00:02:07.954
Zann introduced Ello to his friends.

28
00:02:07.955 --> 00:02:11.345
"Where are you taking us?" Perda asked Ello.

29
00:02:11.346 --> 00:02:15.581
"Our island." Ello pointed ahead. "We'll be there soon."

30
00:02:15.582 --> 00:02:22.268
Zann squinted into the driving rain. He could barely see a small lump on the horizon.

31
00:02:22.269 --> 00:02:25.781
"Is that the island? Where's the mainland?"

32
00:02:25.782 --> 00:02:33.312
Ello shook his head sadly. "There is no mainland anymore. Not since the seas started rising."

33
00:02:33.313 --> 00:02:39.352
"Ello!" someone shouted. "We need your help with the mainsail."

34
00:02:39.353 --> 00:02:42.102
Ello hurried off to help the other fishermen.

35
00:02:42.103 --> 00:02:49.482
Zann and his friends tried to stay out of the way, and soon the boat landed on the rough, rocky shore of the tiny island.

36
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:53.713
About a dozen people were waiting to help drag the sailboat onto the beach.

37
00:02:53.714 --> 00:03:01.766
Ello and the others quickly explained the situation, and Zann and his friends were surrounded by welcoming faces.

38
00:03:01.767 --> 00:03:11.353
"Come inside—you're soaked," a kind-faced woman said, gesturing toward a handful of humble wooden huts on stilts clustered nearby.

39
00:03:11.354 --> 00:03:16.612
"Ello! Find our visitors some dry clothes and stoke the fire."

40
00:03:16.613 --> 00:03:20.996
"Yes, Mother," Ello replied, running ahead up the beach.

41
00:03:20.997 --> 00:03:26.849
Soon Zann and his friends were climbing a rough rope ladder into the largest hut.

42
00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:32.668
It felt good to get out of the constant wind and rain, though it was still damp and chilly inside.

43
00:03:32.669 --> 00:03:38.148
The fire sputtering in the center of the main room offered little light and even less heat.

44
00:03:38.149 --> 00:03:41.501
Most of the people from the beach crowded into the hut.

45
00:03:41.502 --> 00:03:48.516
Ello's mother poured warm drinks from a kettle resting in the embers and passed a mug to each visitor.

46
00:03:48.517 --> 00:03:52.169
"Please make yourselves at home," she said.

47
00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:58.249
"Thank you," Zann said. The drink tasted strange, but it made him feel warm.

48
00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:01.533
"And thank you for rescuing us," Perda added.

49
00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:04.443
"What were those creatures that attacked us?"

50
00:04:04.444 --> 00:04:08.246
"You mean the gulpers?" One of the men looked surprised.

51
00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:13.551
"How can you not know them? They're the most dangerous beasts in all of Skellia."

52
00:04:13.552 --> 00:04:18.438
"Skellia? Is that the name of this land?" asked Gliss.

53
00:04:18.439 --> 00:04:22.128
"We're not from here. We came through a wormhole."

54
00:04:22.129 --> 00:04:25.644
Another man gasped. "From the vortex?"

55
00:04:25.645 --> 00:04:30.076
Immediately the Skellians started whispering among themselves.

56
00:04:30.077 --> 00:04:34.986
"Are you from a land of magic?" a woman asked, leaning forward.

57
00:04:34.987 --> 00:04:42.240
"Yes," Zann said. "Isn't this a magical land too? Our magic seems to work here."

58
00:04:42.241 --> 00:04:48.993
Perda nodded, rubbed her hands together, and pointed at the fire. "Increase!" she said.

59
00:04:48.994 --> 00:04:54.666
The fire grew bigger and hotter. The Skellians gasped with amazement.

60
00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:57.187
Perda smiled. "See?"

61
00:04:57.188 --> 00:05:01.608
"That explains why the gulpers were after you," one of the fishermen said.

62
00:05:01.609 --> 00:05:07.111
"What do you mean?" Zann was confused. "What is this place?"

63
00:05:07.112 --> 00:05:13.366
Taking turns, their hosts finished explaining what Ello had started to tell them in the boat.

64
00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:20.962
Over the past few generations, most of the land in Skellia had been swallowed up by rough, rising seas.

65
00:05:20.963 --> 00:05:24.233
The people of Skellia had weak and limited magic.

66
00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:27.970
They couldn't do much more than conjure food and fresh water.

67
00:05:27.971 --> 00:05:33.984
Even working together, they were unable to stop the seas or create more land.

68
00:05:33.985 --> 00:05:39.992
"That's why everyone is desperate to escape to other worlds before all the land is gone," Ello said.

69
00:05:39.993 --> 00:05:45.045
"The trouble is the gulpers. They're attracted to magic energy—they feed on it.

70
00:05:45.046 --> 00:05:48.772
And there's no stronger magic in Skellia than a wormhole."

71
00:05:48.773 --> 00:05:55.218
A woman nodded. "Every time one pops into existence, the gulpers quickly gulp it down."

72
00:05:55.219 --> 00:06:00.597
"You mean they eat the wormholes?" Gliss exclaimed.

73
00:06:00.598 --> 00:06:09.843
"They swallow them whole." Ello shrugged. "Unless a wormhole happens to pop up on land, it's nearly impossible to reach one before a gulper finds it."

74
00:06:09.844 --> 00:06:18.861
"For instance," a fisherman said, "those gulpers you saw have probably swallowed the wormhole you came through."

75
00:06:18.862 --> 00:06:23.227
Zann stared at his friends as they all realized what this meant.

76
00:06:23.228 --> 00:06:29.678
They were trapped in this world, just like the natives!

